Decomposition: breaking a big problem into smaller sub-problems that are easier to solve, then combining their solutions.
Example: 'organise a school sports day' → plan events, prepare the field, register athletes, record results, award prizes.
Solutions can be represented as:
• structure diagrams (showing the sub-problems);
• algorithms in plain steps;
• pseudocode (structured English-like statements);
• flowcharts (diagrams with standard symbols).
Each part should have clear inputs, processing and outputs (IPO).
